WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.320
Default credentials, sample accounts, and vendor defaults are common attack targets.

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:11.380
Any default identity, password, token, or administrative path should be removed, changed,

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:14.160
or tightly controlled before production use.

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:20.140
Open cloud storage and permissive access policies can expose sensitive records, exports,

00:00:20.360 --> 00:00:23.240
backups, logs, or artifacts.

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:26.980
Cloud configuration must be treated as part of application security.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:29.840
Excessive services increase attack surface.

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:35.580
Every enabled service, plugin, port, feature flag, debug endpoint,

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:39.560
and administrative function should have a documented purpose and owner.

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:45.540
Insecure defaults and debug interfaces may reveal stack traces, paths, secrets,

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:48.480
environment details, and internal architecture.

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:53.180
Diagnostic information belongs in protected logs, not public responses.

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:58.680
Use hardened baselines for applications, systems, containers, and cloud services.

00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:02.100
Manage configuration through reviewed and repeatable processes.

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:06.560
Apply least functionality by disabling unnecessary services and features.

00:01:06.780 --> 00:01:14.620
Selected CMMC mappings for this topic include CM.L2-3.4.1 - Baseline configurations;

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:19.960
CM.L2-3.4.2 - Secure configurations.
